  [OK] lib/sbi/sbi_domain_context.c:137-140  switch_to_next_domain_context
      The __sbi_sfence_vma_all() at line 140 is correctly placed immediately after csr_swap(CSR_SATP, ...) at line 139, satisfying the RISC-V ISA requirement (clarified in riscv-isa-manual PR #2219) that SFENCE.VMA must intervene between an satp.MODE change and any subsequent virtual-address translation. Without this fence, hardware may use cached translations from the old domain's address-width, creating a cross-domain TLB-leak primitive. The implementation of __sbi_sfence_vma_all() at sbi_tlb.c:32 issues a bare 'sfence.vma' inline-asm with appropriate compiler memory clobber, which the ISA guarantees will synchronize page-table walks. No TOCTOU window exists because the csr_swap is an atomic read-modify-write and the fence follows in the next instruction with no intervening memory dereference.
  [RISK] lib/sbi/sbi_domain_context.c:193-227  sbi_domain_context_enter
      sbi_domain_context_enter is the sole public entry point for moving a hart into a target domain. It validates that the target domain is non-null and different from the current domain (line 200), ensures a context exists per hart per domain (lines 208-216), and then delegates to switch_to_next_domain_context. Critically, this function performs zero attestation-related checks: it does not verify that the target domain's measurement matches a signed attestation payload, does not validate a MAC over a TAP, does not require a lockbox-wrapped TSK bound to the platform's identity key, and does not inspect or reject unsupported attributes. Any caller can pass an arbitrary struct sbi_domain* and gain entry to that domain's address space. The security invariant 'only an attested-and-authorized TVM is entered via this path' is entirely caller-enforced with no in-code assertion, gate, or cryptographic binding. This makes the entire local-attestation secret-provisioning chain fail-open: if the higher-layer attestation verification is skipped, buggy, or bypassed, this function will silently switch the hart into an unauthorized domain's page tables with no audit trail.

